{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts","id":431943,"title":"Hunting Grounds Thoughts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-07T16:18:04-08:00","id":431943,"title":"Hunting Grounds Thoughts","content":"I am currently reading through the Hunting Grounds, and I admit the formatting of them is a little irksome. One ends, and then another begins, on the same page.<br /> <br /> They are also somewhat sparse, though this is also probably a blessing - it serves as the seed from which a GM can flesh out a larger setting.<br /> <br /> I am still reading them, but the positive things I have to say: They really are inspiring and creative. They aren't afraid to challenge the status quo described in the rest of the book for the sake of creating interesting conflict.<br /> <br /> Overall I'd say they are something of a success. I might comment on specific Hunting Grounds later.<br /> <br /> Does anyone else have any thoughts on how these were done, or about any Hunting Grounds in particular?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T05:42:25-07:00","id":433815,"title":"","content":"Well, I can say that I had a lot of fun writing the Bristol and the Lower Silesia Hunting Grounds <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A side-note - Last Rites in the fiction anthology ties into the Bristol setting, and I believe one of the other stories ties into the Alice Springs setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:41:12-07:00","id":434587,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, Lower Silesia is one of my favorites from the whole bunch! The Lodge of the Field may be my most favorite Uratha heresy, and I love what look at the setting Lycaon-Ur gives us. My own preference is that he's a very ancient and bizarre Primal Urge 10 werewolf, but other possibilities aren't off-putting either.<br /> <br /> Basra was also a big one for me. A city with only a single tribe and some Ghost Wolves? That's just crazy in the good way; there's a mystery and a conflict there, and there's value both in exploring being part of the increasingly erratic Blood Talon majority or the mysteriously oppressed Ghost Wolves.<br /> <br /> Tokyo of course was wonderful because I could use it to fill out yet another piece of my greater Tokyo crossover setting. I wasn't expecting so many ghost wolves and packless, but I love how much was tied into Japan's indigenous peoples and their beliefs.<br /> <br /> Alice Springs was as good this time around as it was when we saw it on the blog: it made me want to play in Australia.<br /> <br /> And someone made a setting full of Amish very intriguing without caricatures. Props for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T15:12:42-07:00","id":434645,"title":"","content":"Speaking of, I'm going to be barreling into an Ohio game soon. These settings seem to be real boons for new Storytellers. Bless the chapter and the confidence it gives to them! Bwahahah!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T18:28:47-07:00","id":434991,"title":"","content":"Basra is more then that. Fenris himself is there. I suspect he's found his mate, and the ghost wolves are there to be her tribe. Read not oppression. But that they aren't allowed to leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T19:23:45-07:00","id":435110,"title":"","content":"My favorite Hunting Ground is Tokyo. I love the stetting and the werewolf origin story, awesome. Who knew the strix (Tengu) were willing to work with the Uratha. Ha ha that must suck for the vampires in Tokyo. The shrines were another great detail and how most of them are protected by the Uratha, mainly because there locies. I'm just completely captivated by the setting. I hope the writers write more on Tokyo or any Japanese setting in future supplements. That's why I'm crossing my fingers for werewolf samurai era in Dark Eras--samurai werewolves baby! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Oh! And applause to the writer/s who created Tokyo Hunting Ground. Thank you so much!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T20:16:30-07:00","id":435191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=434991#post434991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basra is more then that. Fenris himself is there. I suspect he's found his mate, and the ghost wolves are there to be her tribe. Read not oppression. But that they aren't allowed to leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am aware of these things!<br /> <br /> Their motive for keeping the ghost wolves there in no way lessens the oppressive element involved in keeping the ghost wolves there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T20:20:41-07:00","id":435194,"title":"","content":"That's true. I thought you just meant is was a cast system in the city imposed by the Talons. I love that the proximity of Fenris is slowly driving the Talons insane. Brings home that the firstborn are basically gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T20:22:53-07:00","id":435198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=435194#post435194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true. I thought you just meant is was a cast system in the city imposed by the Talons. I love that the proximity of Fenris is slowly driving the Talons insane. Brings home that the firstborn are basically gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's certainly a <i>de facto</i> caste system: they're on top, everyone else is either out or forced to stay there and keep their heads down until something changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T01:01:52-07:00","id":435449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=434587#post434587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basra was also a big one for me. A city with only a single tribe and some Ghost Wolves? That's just crazy in the good way; there's a mystery and a conflict there, and there's value both in exploring being part of the increasingly erratic Blood Talon majority or the mysteriously oppressed Ghost Wolves.<br /> <br /> ...snip...<br /> <br /> Alice Springs was as good this time around as it was when we saw it on the blog: it made me want to play in Australia.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here makes it all worth while <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit: And people digging Basra and seeing all the mad potential there is icing on the cake!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 03-10-2015, 04:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T01:21:14-07:00","id":435457,"title":"","content":"Bunyip... How did I know you were at the heart of this!?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T02:03:12-07:00","id":435478,"title":"","content":"Because it's broken in all the right ways? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Bonus internet cookie if you can guess the other bits I did - but probably not through polluting this thread. PM me with answers.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T05:13:51-07:00","id":435552,"title":"","content":"Basra is my favourite of the Hunting Grounds That Are Not Mine (tm). It's intriguing, it's unique, and it plugs into Werewolf mythology in a fantastic way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:06:21-07:00","id":435572,"title":"","content":"One thing I enjoyed was the mention in the Belfast setting that lands without surviving wolf populations in the modern day still have uralath populations in the Hisil. Partially because The Buddy Spirit is my favorite spiritual touchstone and it would suck to be deprived of that because I was playing in Japan or the British Isles, but also partially because it means I can more readily embrace my character idea for a Tokyo game.<br /> <br /> The Hunter in Darkness whose lineage has sworn an oath to the wolf spirits to avenge the extinction of the Honshu wolf. If Japan were a bit more into the whole tribe thing they'd have probably jumped ship to Predator Kings a while back ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:09:18-07:00","id":435576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=435110#post435110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite Hunting Ground is Tokyo. I love the stetting and the werewolf origin story, awesome. Who knew the strix (Tengu) were willing to work with the Uratha. Ha ha that must suck for the vampires in Tokyo. The shrines were another great detail and how most of them are protected by the Uratha, mainly because there locies. I'm just completely captivated by the setting. I hope the writers write more on Tokyo or any Japanese setting in future supplements. That's why I'm crossing my fingers for werewolf samurai era in Dark Eras--samurai werewolves baby! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Oh! And applause to the writer/s who created Tokyo Hunting Ground. Thank you so much!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much! Turns out, I will be developing the Japan setting for Dark Eras as well as my other Tokyo bits across the various books. I can't tell anyone what it'll be yet though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T06:20:11-07:00","id":435584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=435576#post435576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you so much! Turns out, I will be developing the Japan setting for Dark Eras as well as my other Tokyo bits across the various books. I can't tell anyone what it'll be yet though.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean besides heavily influenced by Samurai Champloo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:48:49-07:00","id":436064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=435576#post435576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you so much! Turns out, I will be developing the Japan setting for Dark Eras as well as my other Tokyo bits across the various books. I can't tell anyone what it'll be yet though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice! I cannot wait! If you don't mind me asking, will you or OP be announcing which game line got samurai era? I really hope it's werewolf. He he he... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean besides heavily influenced by Samurai Champloo?</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Samurai Champloo! It was that anime that inspired me to love Japan's history and culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:25:49-07:00","id":436444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=435584#post435584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean besides heavily influenced by Samurai Champloo?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. <br /> <br /> My Samurai Champloo inspired pitch for Dark Eras didn't actually get picked. Truth be told, I'm not even sure what I'm doing for this piece yet, since it's set in a specific and sort of weird time that's a little more antiquated than my area of expertise. But, I'm excited to toy with it once I find out the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T17:34:16-07:00","id":436453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=436444#post436444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well.<br /> <br /> My Samurai Champloo inspired pitch for Dark Eras didn't actually get picked. Truth be told, I'm not even sure what I'm doing for this piece yet, since it's set in a specific and sort of weird time that's a little more antiquated than my area of expertise. But, I'm excited to toy with it once I find out the details.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, I was looking forward to that one ...<br /> <br /> Oh well; I'm sure you'll figure something great out by the time you need to write it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T19:12:19-07:00","id":436544,"title":"","content":"I liked Basra, a whole city dominated by Blood talons which drove out all other forsaken shows that the tribes can fight each other quite a bit.<br /> <br /> I also liked Ohio. If you can have Werewolves in Amish country you can have them anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T20:25:31-07:00","id":436615,"title":"","content":"I'm glad people are enjoying the Ohio setting. I thought a back-to-nature kinda place would be nice for 2E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>John Newman<br /> Onyx Path Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5213-jn7","name":"JN7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T21:00:08-07:00","id":436639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JN7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=436615#post436615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad people are enjoying the Ohio setting. I thought a back-to-nature kinda place would be nice for 2E.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf is one of the lines that I most enjoy the prospect of rural settings for, so thanks for providing one for us!<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness there is a strong bias toward settings focused on urban areas, so seeing something ... less so is great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T21:26:56-07:00","id":436652,"title":"","content":"Part of the appeal to forsaken vs apocalypse for me. Forsaken always felt more... Werewolf then apocalypse did. So much of it jives better then apocalypses world for the old world mythos of forsaken. I feel like I have more creative freedom with nwod as a whole, but forsaken feels like it has teeth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T05:46:00-07:00","id":436921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=436639#post436639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf is one of the lines that I most enjoy the prospect of rural settings for, so thanks for providing one for us!<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness there is a strong bias toward settings focused on urban areas, so seeing something ... less so is great.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interesting thing to balance, yeah. It's one reason why I had the Field of Dogs cover Lower Silesia rather than just Wroclaw, as a counterpoint to the very urban-focused Bristol Hunting Ground. Though even Bristol has some reach into both the surrounding countryside and more unusual areas such as the water itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T06:14:22-07:00","id":436960,"title":"","content":"Did the Hunting Grounds team ever come across an idea for an area that just seemed... Lame? Like there was nothing you could do to get excited about New Jersey no matter what you did? :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T06:43:41-07:00","id":436993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=436960#post436960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the Hunting Grounds team ever come across an idea for an area that just seemed... Lame? Like there was nothing you could do to get excited about New Jersey no matter what you did? :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think we all just picked the areas we wanted to do then pitched them to Stew, rather than having it dictated to us what areas we should do.<br /> <br /> I <i>did</i> have other Hunting Grounds I'd have loved to do if there'd been space for more - Bangkok in Thailand and Gevaudan in France. Managed to slip a little bit about Gevaudan in anyway, via the Quicksilver Children, which indicates what the set-up would have been for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:01:21-07:00","id":437090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=435552#post435552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basra is my favourite of the Hunting Grounds That Are Not Mine (tm). It's intriguing, it's unique, and it plugs into Werewolf mythology in a fantastic way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Basra is also my favorite of the Hunting Grounds. While reading it I got stuck on the impression that Destroyer Wolf has had the Blood Talon's turn the city into one giant crock pot. With the Ghost Wolves left to stew, in the hopes that they'll find a certain passageway in the Hisil.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Also the fact that a additional (tribeless) First Born is mentioned on the first page of the write up as nothing to do with my interest... and the fact that the only group that can create a new tribe is the Ghost Wolves.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yup, totally my favorite, [sarcasm] while being totally empty of plot hooks. [/sarcasm] <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T09:04:32-07:00","id":437092,"title":"","content":"Bangkok would have been cool too, I don't know anything about Gevaudan aside from what was in Brotherhood of the Wolf. I think there's a bed and breakfast there.<br /> <br /> I'm really liking Basra, too. One of the areas is well within the domain of my upcoming game so I'm hesitant to read it in case of spoilers. I've left the Hunting Ground section for last but I'm finally buckling and getting into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T10:56:57-07:00","id":437234,"title":"","content":"Gevaudan played host to the events and hysteria around the supposed 'Beast of Gevaudan', one of those seminal moments relating to wolves and folklore in the 1700s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T11:04:27-07:00","id":437238,"title":"","content":"Yeah the movie was a dramatized account of that, with madmen and femme fatales thrown in. I just meant beyond that. Apparently it ceased to exist as a county and is now <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loz%C3%A8re\" target=\"_blank\">Loz\u00e8re</a>, though the terrain looks great for werewolfian adventures, with mountains and caves and a lot of forests.<br /> <br /> Reading Bristol now, I like the deal with the Protectorate and how it's affecting the werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T16:03:26-07:00","id":437674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=436993#post436993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we all just picked the areas we wanted to do then pitched them to Stew, rather than having it dictated to us what areas we should do.<br /> <br /> I <i>did</i> have other Hunting Grounds I'd have loved to do if there'd been space for more - Bangkok in Thailand and Gevaudan in France. Managed to slip a little bit about Gevaudan in anyway, via the Quicksilver Children, which indicates what the set-up would have been for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Gevaudan would have been amazeballs!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T19:15:51-07:00","id":439233,"title":"","content":"I just got through all of the Hunting Grounds today, and wow they're filled with awesome stuff. I'm not sure which one is my favorite.<br /> <br /> To mention specific things I found interesting even though they're less central though: the Voyagers. Deceived scorpion cult, anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T22:42:10-07:00","id":439423,"title":"","content":"I gotta admit, I ran around for like 10 minutes straight, cheering at the Detroit and Ohio Settings. I live 10 minutes outside of Detroit, and have an close family who live in Holmes county, so those settings were especially poignant to me. I was impressed with how tactful the Detroit setting was written, it would have been way too easy to rip on the more recent political scandals and focus on the negatives of the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T15:33:58-07:00","id":440525,"title":"","content":"Glad you enjoyed the settings!<br /> <br /> I had a friend that grew up in Detroit help me get as close to the proper feel as I could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>John Newman<br /> Onyx Path Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5213-jn7","name":"JN7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5213_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T10:22:19-07:00","id":441546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=434587#post434587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh hey, Lower Silesia is one of my favorites from the whole bunch! The Lodge of the Field may be my most favorite Uratha heresy, and I love what look at the setting Lycaon-Ur gives us. My own preference is that he's a very ancient and bizarre Primal Urge 10 werewolf, but other possibilities aren't off-putting either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also like &quot;Dolny \u015al\u0105sk&quot; setting, not only because it's in mine country. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Blashpemous werewolf cults were always mine thing. Only those spellings of Polish words... Well, I hope they fix that before final book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=434587#post434587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basra was also a big one for me. A city with only a single tribe and some Ghost Wolves? That's just crazy in the good way; there's a mystery and a conflict there, and there's value both in exploring being part of the increasingly erratic Blood Talon majority or the mysteriously oppressed Ghost Wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree! It also great excuse for sending NATO troops on werewolf hunt... eee, terrorist searching? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=434587#post434587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tokyo of course was wonderful because I could use it to fill out yet another piece of my greater Tokyo crossover setting. I wasn't expecting so many ghost wolves and packless, but I love how much was tied into Japan's indigenous peoples and their beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is I'm a bit disappointed. First, <i>why</i> there is no pack culture in town? <i>Why</i> no real Tribal presence? I get it's unique setting that &quot;we all are lone wolves here&quot;, but I would want at least a clue of why Tribes of Moon do not fully developed here. In Australia, there is mentioned that Lodge of Dreaming did not need the Tribes, and they come with white colonist. Okay, I can get that Tribes of Moon are European working - but still, Japan was having those contacts at least from the 1500's - enough for some adaptation.<br /> <br /> I could see that Forsaken society has crisis from the times of end from Meiji Restoration, and packs were disbanded after samurai cast and local wolf breed died out - but I would at least want a hint of what happened so the Tokyo is as it is.<br /> <br /> Also, why <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tsukuyomi-no-Mikoto\" target=\"_blank\">Tsukuyomi</a> is not mentioned as alternate Moon parent for other Uratha groups in setting? And why not be progressive and let both Wolf and Moon be male in Uratha myths? Ancient Rome Uratha have Two Mothers, Japanese cannot have Two Fathers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( It was, partially, a joke. Partially ) On the other hand, corebook mentions that werewolves are gender fluid species...<br /> <br /> <b>And I did not get mine <a href=\"http://godzilla.wikia.com/wiki/Category:Monsters\" target=\"_blank\">Daikaiju</a> destroying Tokyo Tower every week or so!</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-15-2015, 03:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T18:19:10-07:00","id":443461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=441546#post441546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also like &quot;Dolny \u015al\u0105sk&quot; setting, not only because it's in mine country. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Blashpemous werewolf cults were always mine thing. Only those spellings of Polish words... Well, I hope they fix that before final book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The issues with certain letters in the Field of Dogs setting are down to the font etc being used in the book; they're all spelled correctly in the drafts, but the layout kinda obliterated a bunch of the Polish lettering.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this may not be something that can be easily solved and I guess some of the Polish words may be simplified as a result. I would love to have all the \u0142's and so forth in there, but sadly the Polish language is just too awesome for the software to cope with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T21:38:08-07:00","id":443715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=443461#post443461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issues with certain letters in the Field of Dogs setting are down to the font etc being used in the book; they're all spelled correctly in the drafts, but the layout kinda obliterated a bunch of the Polish lettering.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately this may not be something that can be easily solved and I guess some of the Polish words may be simplified as a result. I would love to have all the \u0142's and so forth in there, but sadly the Polish language is just too awesome for the software to cope with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Understand that. The bigger problem is using inccorect gramatic case in text, if polish diacritics are no to be in PDF from software position. &quot;Wilkolakow&quot; instead of &quot;wilkolaki&quot; and &quot;kikimory&quot; instead &quot;kikimora&quot;, when sentantace context point to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-16-2015, 12:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T22:17:18-07:00","id":443743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/431943-hunting-grounds-thoughts?p=439423#post439423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gotta admit, I ran around for like 10 minutes straight, cheering at the Detroit and Ohio Settings. I live 10 minutes outside of Detroit, and have an close family who live in Holmes county, so those settings were especially poignant to me. I was impressed with how tactful the Detroit setting was written, it would have been way too easy to rip on the more recent political scandals and focus on the negatives of the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>I live in Lansing and yeah, its easy to latch onto the &quot;cesspool&quot; of Detroit, but really, what's left of the city's populous is hopeful. There are still innumerable problems but people seem to actually want to fix them. Its awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}